<!--
  Pocket Prose's launcher icon: three sheets of paper, seen from above and slightly to one side.

  Generated from assets/icon_mk1.svg, which is the editable source and lives beside this repository
  rather than in it. Re-export from there; do not hand-edit the path data below.

  The source is artwork on transparency with no ground of its own — an adaptive icon keeps its
  ground in a separate layer, so that colour lives in values/ic_launcher_background.xml. The two
  must be changed together.

  SIZE. This is the number that has been got wrong twice, so read the whole paragraph before
  changing it. The layers are 108dp, but a launcher only ever shows the **centre 72dp** — the outer
  18dp on each side is bleed for parallax and masking. So the tile you see is 72dp, not 108, and any
  scale reasoned against 108 comes out half again too big. The artwork here is 58dp wide,
  which is 81% of that visible tile.

  Rubber Ring's is 69.7dp, or 97% — but its mark is square (69.7 x 69.0) and fills the tile in both
  directions, so filling it reads as deliberate. This drawing is 1.2:1, so matching that ratio filled
  the width exactly while leaving air above and below, and read as stretched edge to edge. A wide
  mark needs a margin that a square one does not.

  CENTRING. The offsets subtract the drawing's own origin inside its canvas (73, 127) as
  well as splitting what is left over. Halving the remainder alone is not centring — it shifts the
  art by the origin, invisibly at large sizes and plainly at small ones. That bug shipped once.

  Re-measure X0/Y0/W/H by rendering the source and taking its bounding box if the artwork changes;
  they are facts about the file, not constants.
-->
